      ],
      "text": "Questions 6-13\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        70.90567779541016,
        110.49771881103516,
        511.7808532714844,
        121.30638885498047
      ],
      "text": "Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        70.9056625366211,
        138.5720672607422,
        292.2609558105469,
        149.38067626953125
      ],
      "text": "In boxes 6—13 on your answer sheet, write\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        110.13771057128906,
        165.9265594482422,
        411.77496337890625,
        202.28787231445312
      ],
      "text": "TRUE\nif the statement agrees with the information\nFALSE\nif the statement contradicts the information\nNOT GIVEN\nif there is no information on this\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        77.02436065673828,
        229.27378845214844,
        521.8802490234375,
        240.4426727294922
      ],
      "text": "6\nSignificant numbers of thylacines were killed by humans from the 1830s onwards.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        77.0243911743164,
        250.50950622558594,
        404.6086730957031,
        261.67840576171875
      ],
      "text": "7\nSeveral thylacines were born in zoos during the late 1800s.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        77.0243911743164,
        272.4650573730469,
        461.1572570800781,
        283.27374267578125
      ],
      "text": "8\nJohn Gould’s prediction about the thylacine surprised some biologists.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        77.02442169189453,
        294.0606994628906,
        531.5767822265625,
        318.906494140625
      ],
      "text": "9\nInthe early 1900s, many scientists became worried about the possible extinction of\nthe thylacine.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        70.90565490722656,
        329.6935119628906,
        495.8720397949219,
        340.5021667480469
      ],
      "text": "10\nT.T. Flynn’s proposal to rehome captive thylacines on an island proved to be\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        96.82041931152344,
        343.730712890625,
        155.1286163330078,
        354.5393371582031
      ],
      "text": "impractical.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        70.90564727783203,
        363.88665771484375,
        508.9049377441406,
        377.9378356933594
      ],
      "text": "11\nThere were still reasonable numbers of thylacines in existence when a piece of\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        96.82041931152344,
        379.3634948730469,
        488.5115661621094,
        390.1721496582031
      ],
      "text": "legislation protecting the species during their breeding season was passed.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        70.9056625366211,
        400.95916748046875,
        471.8287353515625,
        412.1280822753906
      ],
      "text": "12\nFrom 1930 to 1936, the only known living thylacines were all in captivity.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        70.90569305419922,
        422.5548400878906,
        377.6539001464844,
        433.7237548828125
      ],
      "text": "13\nAttempts to find living thylacines are now rarely made.\n"
    },
